{
  "page": 69,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Discussion on the Paper by Andrieu, Doucet and Holenstein",
      "bbox": [
        170.1251983642578,
        39.52751922607422,
        407.9410095214844,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "337",
      "bbox": [
        428.84710693359375,
        39.52751922607422,
        443.8030700683594,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "when applicable, seem at ﬁrst appealing. They are particularly elegant in scenarios where p.θ|x1:T , y1:T /",
      "bbox": [
        48.089813232421875,
        56.625526428222656,
        443.6011962890625,
        67.035400390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "depends on x1:T , y1:T only through a set of ﬁxed dimensional statistics and have received signiﬁcant atten-",
      "bbox": [
        48.08880615234375,
        67.34110260009766,
        443.6053771972656,
        76.99810791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion since their introduction and development over a decade ago; see for example Andrieu et al. (1999,",
      "bbox": [
        48.08937072753906,
        77.3038101196289,
        443.6017761230469,
        85.61566162109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2005), Fearnhead (1998, 2002), Storvik (2002) and Vercauteren et al. (2005). Despite their appeal these",
      "bbox": [
        48.08935546875,
        87.26639556884766,
        443.6035461425781,
        95.5782470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "well-documented methods are widely acknowledged to be rather delicate to use, owing to the so-called",
      "bbox": [
        48.089385986328125,
        97.2289810180664,
        443.6045227050781,
        105.54083251953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "path degeneracy phenomenon and the fact that a good initialization distribution for θ seems paramount",
      "bbox": [
        48.089385986328125,
        106.43839263916016,
        443.6017150878906,
        115.50341796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "because of the lack of ergodicity of the system. In fact such techniques rely implicitly on the approximation",
      "bbox": [
        48.0885009765625,
        117.1541519165039,
        443.60443115234375,
        125.46600341796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of p.x1:T |y1:T / and it can be observed empirically that the algorithm might converge to incorrect values and",
      "bbox": [
        48.0885009765625,
        126.3639907836914,
        443.60748291015625,
        136.67523193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "even sometimes drift away from the correct values as the time index T increases; see for example Andrieu",
      "bbox": [
        48.089744567871094,
        137.0797576904297,
        443.60211181640625,
        145.3916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al. (1999, 2005).",
      "bbox": [
        48.089752197265625,
        147.04234313964844,
        117.76763916015625,
        155.35418701171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As a consequence we would recommend extreme caution when using such techniques, whose interest",
      "bbox": [
        57.056148529052734,
        157.0049285888672,
        443.6048583984375,
        165.3167724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "might be to provide a quick initial guess for the inference problem at hand. Assessing path degeneracy is",
      "bbox": [
        48.08974838256836,
        166.96751403808594,
        443.60028076171875,
        175.27935791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "certainly essential to evaluate the credibility of the results. A simple proxy to measure degeneracy consists",
      "bbox": [
        48.08974838256836,
        176.9300994873047,
        443.6100769042969,
        185.241943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of monitoring the number of distinct particles representing p.xk|y1:T / for various values of k ∈{1, . . . , T}",
      "bbox": [
        48.08974838256836,
        186.1397705078125,
        443.6024169921875,
        195.91905212402344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(preferably low values). If this number is below a reasonable number, say 500, then the particle approxi-",
      "bbox": [
        48.089111328125,
        196.8555145263672,
        443.61334228515625,
        205.1673583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mation of p.θ, x1:T |y1:T / is most probably unreliable.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089111328125,
        206.06488037109375,
        245.09500122070312,
        216.37637329101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Johannes, Polson and Yae propose to reconsider the example that was discussed in Section 3.1 and",
      "bbox": [
        57.056175231933594,
        216.7808074951172,
        443.60211181640625,
        225.0926513671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to estimate the parameters .α, σ, β1, β2, β3, σx/. They use Gibbs steps within a bootstrap particle ﬁlter to",
      "bbox": [
        48.08977508544922,
        225.99017333984375,
        443.6025085449219,
        235.7698516845703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "update θ :=.σ, β1, β2, β3, σx/ and a slice sampler to update α. As we do not have the details of their slice",
      "bbox": [
        48.08918762207031,
        235.9530029296875,
        443.6026611328125,
        245.7324676513672
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampler, we shall limit ourselves to the estimation of p.θ, x1:T |y1:T / by using the PG sampler. We considered",
      "bbox": [
        48.089141845703125,
        245.91561889648438,
        443.605224609375,
        256.22705078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their scenario and simulated T =100 data points by using the parameters that Johannes, Polson and Yae",
      "bbox": [
        48.08918762207031,
        255.87820434570312,
        443.6043395996094,
        264.9432373046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "used and we set informative priors approximately similar to theirs by checking the width of their posteriors",
      "bbox": [
        48.08830261230469,
        266.59393310546875,
        443.6033020019531,
        274.9057922363281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "at time n=0. In this context, Johannes, Polson and Yae used 300000 particles for the particle ﬁlter with",
      "bbox": [
        48.08830261230469,
        275.8033142089844,
        443.6087646484375,
        284.86834716796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gibbs moves and argue, on the grounds of the simulations that were discussed at the end of Section 3.1,",
      "bbox": [
        48.08831024169922,
        286.51904296875,
        443.6105041503906,
        294.8309020996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that PMCMC methods would require l000 times more computation to perform inference in this scenario.",
      "bbox": [
        48.08831024169922,
        296.4815979003906,
        443.604248046875,
        304.79345703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We want to reassure them and the readers that this is not so. We used N = 5000 particles at the end of",
      "bbox": [
        48.08831024169922,
        305.69097900390625,
        443.599853515625,
        314.7560119628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
